      "note": "Reviewed anchor, root cause, loss, artifact identity and complete age history. GPv2Settlement 0x9008d19f58aabd9ed0d60971565aa8510560ab41 holds the depleted reserves. The defective artifact is the GlueX helper, not settlement code. Disassemble its 2128-byte runtime: selectors 0xfa461e33 and 0x23a69e75 share the callback at PC 0x03d9. Decode its 128-byte data as a limit, payer, token and pool. CALLER at 0x03fc is compared with the decoded pool at 0x0406. Both positive-delta branches call the transferFrom helper at 0x04c3, which sends tokens from the decoded payer to CALLER at CALL 0x0508. There is no independently authenticated pool or active-swap binding. Source-1 callTracer shows a standalone callback by attacker contract 0x5b5a0580bcfd3673820bb249514234afad33e209, supplying itself as pool and settlement as payer, and successful DRAGONX transferFrom. Source-3 receipt anchors direct CREATE by the declared creator. eth_getCode is empty at block 21114225 and hashes identically at 21114226 and 21135422. Source-1 prestateTracer has the same runtime. Its executable paths have no storage, delegatecall, code-replacement or destruction operations, so allowances affect exposure without resetting age. For earliest-use and loss coverage, run trace_filter toAddress=[helper] over blocks 21114226..21136000 in intervals of at most 9000 blocks, count=10000. It returns 94 frames in 74 transactions: seven legitimate settlement executions, 66 successful standalone drain transactions in source-5, and reverted attempt 0x13a3c4341dac2d1503ec542300e6eb0e0b585011868d022cced1cbb89c354627. No earlier helper call precedes normal settlement execution 0xd011c1f1cfeffaccee3facaf4dd7049a3688d945b01be854a0e75a907ef02fcf at block 21135367. Source-1 is the earliest drain, 15 blocks before the seed anchor. Receipt Transfer logs and successful callback transferFrom amounts independently sum to all six loss components: 67 reserve transfers across 66 transactions, with no matching reserve inflows or attacker-supplied principal. The final drain is 0xaaa82437c665a0209f7dc9c1aab7f743eaafd9ec6b74261102483df617ef1011 at block 21135610 index 4, timestamp 1730980511. Scan all Approval logs with helper as spender from deployment through block 26113676 in 100000-block intervals: 25 logs, seven tokens, settlement as every owner, no approvals after block 21135612. All seven allowance(settlement,helper) calls at 21135612 return zero. The final revocation is source-9. trace_filter 21136001..21145000 returns no calls. Later coverage is bounded by these zero allowances and the absence of renewed approvals through 26113676. Future updates should scan approvals to this helper for renewed exposure. Source-1 sells the entire 18518972.240927552666087192 DRAGONX for 0.104171149931008392 WETH. Source-8 sells the entire 158686945.262774678842276895 TITANX for 0.054398988989087832 WETH. Each receipt shows the stolen token entering its pool and WETH leaving it. Multiply these proceeds by source-6 WETH/USD 2821.8 at timestamp 1730978277, without subtracting builder payments. Source-6 also supplies weETH/USD 2963.92 at 1730978095 and wstETH/USD 3329.27 at 1730978276. USDC is valued at parity. Historical quote times fall before the final drain."
    },
